# D-93 with item 739 and A3: the host calls its capturing model, whose result is size_t, before its return, and
# the root calls the returned node -- natively the host's call is lmx_call_prim over the model's occurrence with
# a size_t temp, n its hidden input; under the knob (unit_walk_make_adder_model_call_size_t) a CALL of the walked
# host.  The root's call of the node goes through l2_mad_call's size_t variant.  makeAdder 4294967296:
# q = addN(1) = 2^32 + 1; n: q + 1; add(1) = 2^32 + 3.  Entry 7.
fn: makeAdder (size_t: n) fn: (size_t: x) size_t
    fn: addN (size_t: x) size_t
        return: n + x
    size_t: q (addN: 1U)
    n: q + 1U
    return: addN

add: makeAdder 4294967296U
size_t: a (add: 1U)
int: ok 0
if: a = 4294967299U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
